WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.100
Film Courage: Chad how old were you when you
knew you wanted to be an actor?

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.300
Chad Lindberg: I knew I wanted to be an actor
at a very young age.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.064
I was always making movies with a video camera
that was like this big [motions with his hands]

00:00:11.064 --> 00:00:13.250
back in the day.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:19.510
And always putting on skits for my parents
and whoever else would watch.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:23.689
And then as I got into high school and stuff,
I wanted to be a cop, like my Dad.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.070
I wanted to be a police officer.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:31.650
So I went to college and signed up to be a
police officer, the whole nine yards.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.580
And then they were auditioning for a play
in high school and a buddy of mine said to

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.620
me “Hey you should audition!” and I’m
like “Geez…I don’t want to audition.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.620
No way.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.620
No way.”

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.620
He’s like “Come on!

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.620
Audition.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.620
It’s for Guys and Dolls.”

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.710
So I auditioned and I’m not a very good
singer.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.540
I’m a terrible singer, in fact.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:53.800
But I got a small part and I got on stage
and that was when I realized that this was

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.800
what I was good at.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.550
I’m not a sports guy.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.940
I was not a football player in high school.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.110
Acting was my thing.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:06.730
And then once I locked on to that, I knew
at a very young age that this was what I was

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:07.920
going to do.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.290
Nobody was going to tell me different.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:16.510
And looking back 22 years later, I am really
thankful that it happened.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:21.650
It doesn’t happen for a lot of people here
that are trying to break into this crazy industry….so…

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:29.020
Film Courage: That’s interesting because
I know a lot of people who come from families

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.300
of many generations of law enforcement.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.480
When you drive by let’s say a police officer
do you ever think to yourself does it register

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:36.860
in your mind like “Hmmm.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:40.950
That could be me right there” had it not
been for a couple of changes of events in

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:41.950
your life?

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:42.950
Chad Lindberg: No.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:43.950
Because I don’t have that inside of me.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.310
I’m not a guy who is going to take down
another guy.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:55.280
I’m not a guy who can pull a gun and make
a life and death decision.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:00.800
With the exception of a few bad apples, I
have nothing but respect for law enforcement

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:01.870
and what they do.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.940
They are true heroes.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.000
Whenever I see a cop, I think of my dad.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.980
And I think of him putting himself out there
in harm’s way and helping people and being

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.270
respectful to people, treating everyone with
respect.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:20.870
So that’s what I think about when I see
police officers and I’m grateful that we

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:21.870
have them.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:26.760
Film Courage: Did you feel any pressure though,
to take another course?

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:33.300
Chad Lindberg: My parents were 100% supportive
of me from the very beginning.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:38.440
Because they saw…they saw that this was
what I wanted to do and what I was good at.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:43.420
And a lot of actors I’ve talked to didn’t
have parental support.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:48.010
Which makes me sad because that is all I have
is their support.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:51.510
Even to this day they are 100% behind me.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:55.320
If I book something that they are a fan of,
it’s always really exciting.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.540
I remember when I got [a part of the tv show]
E.R. and my mom flipped out because it was

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.780
really big back at the time.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.459
And George Clooney and all of this cool stuff.

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:09.239
Or if there is a cool action movie my Dad
will come and visit me on set.

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:15.939
So they are amazing parents and I’ve been
so lucky to have their support.

00:03:15.939 --> 00:03:22.819
This business is very unforgiving in a lot
of ways in terms of the rejection and the

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:25.620
honesty you get as an actor.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.790
So having that support when you fall down
makes a difference.

